<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-13110] An option to validate field types against SQL schema on key-value insert</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-13110</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Let&apos;s add a configurable option to prevent insertion of key-value pairs that aren&apos;t compatible with SQL schema.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An option can be added on &lt;tt&gt;SqlConfiguration&lt;/tt&gt; level or even per &lt;tt&gt;QueryEntity&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The checks can be performed within the existing &lt;tt&gt;GridQueryTypeDescriptor#validateKeyAndValue&lt;/tt&gt; facility that seems to be well suited for this task.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This addition will prevent the problems when values successfully added to the cache later produce errors when queried with SQL.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;See discussion : &lt;a href=&quot;http://apache-ignite-developers.2346864.n4.nabble.com/Prevent-insertion-of-cache-entry-if-the-binary-field-type-and-the-type-of-the-query-entity-do-not-ma-td47678.html&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://apache-ignite-developers.2346864.n4.nabble.com/Prevent-insertion-of-cache-entry-if-the-binary-field-type-and-the-type-of-the-query-entity-do-not-ma-td47678.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;


